.SH NAME
Plack::Session::State::Cookie \- Basic cookie\-based session state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&  use Plack::Builder;
\&  use Plack::Middleware::Session;
\&
\&  my $app = sub {
\&      return [ 200, [ \*(AqContent\-Type\*(Aq => \*(Aqtext/plain\*(Aq ], [ \*(AqHello Foo\*(Aq ] ];
\&  };
\&
\&  builder {
\&      enable \*(AqSession\*(Aq; # Cookie is the default state
\&      $app;
\&  };
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This is a subclass of Plack::Session::State and implements its
full interface. This is the default state used in
Plack::Middleware::Session.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.ie n .IP "\fBnew ( \fR\fB%params\fR\fB )\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fBnew ( \fR\f(CB%params\fR\fB )\fR" 4
.IX Item "new ( %params )"
The \f(CW%params\fR can include \fIpath\fR, \fIdomain\fR, \fIexpires\fR, \fIsecure\fR,
and \fIhttponly\fR options, as well as all the options accepted by
Plack::Session::State.
.IP \fBpath\fR 4
.IX Item "path"
Path of the cookie, this defaults to "/";
.IP \fBdomain\fR 4
.IX Item "domain"
Domain of the cookie, if nothing is supplied then it will not
be included in the cookie.
.IP \fBexpires\fR 4
.IX Item "expires"
Expiration time of the cookie in seconds, if nothing is supplied then
it will not be included in the cookie, which means the session expires
per browser session.
.IP \fBsecure\fR 4
.IX Item "secure"
Secure flag for the cookie, if nothing is supplied then it will not
be included in the cookie.
.IP \fBhttponly\fR 4
.IX Item "httponly"
HttpOnly flag for the cookie, if nothing is supplied then it will not
be included in the cookie.
.IP \fBsamesite\fR 4
.IX Item "samesite"
SameSite flag for the cookie, if nothing is supplied then it will not
be included in the cookie.
